after prefixes maybe line1 each prefix line.\n\nLet's write quickly: Provide approximate lines. Use location start/end line numbers.\n\nWe can give location line numbers of the problematic statements.\n\nsh:property [ begins line after targetClass.\n\nLet's count: I'll write lines:\n\n1 @prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n2 @prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n3 @prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n4 @prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n5 @prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n6 @prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n7 @prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n8 \n9 # Shape enforcing the requirement TRF‑035 clause 4.1.1:\n10 # “L shall be taken as the ship's rule length used by the classification society.”\n11 # L is represented by the property vocab:ruleLength whose value must be a\n12 # qudt:QuantityValue with a numeric value (decimal) and the unit metre.\n13 \n14 vocab:ShipRuleLengthShape\n15     a sh:NodeShape ;\n16     sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n17     sh:property [\n18         sh:path vocab:ruleLength ;\n19         sh:minCount 1 ;\n20         sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;            # the value must be a node (QuantityValue)\n21         sh:node [\n22             a sh:NodeShape ;\n23             sh:property [\n24                 sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n25                 sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n26                 sh:minCount 1\n27             ] ;\n28             sh:property [\n29                 sh:path qudt:unit ;\n30                 sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n31                 sh:minCount 1\n32             ]\n33         ]\n34     ] .\n\nThus issues at line20 (nodeKind), line21-33 missing class assertion.\n\nProvide suggestions: change nodeKind to sh:BlankNodeOrIRI or remove, add sh:class qudt:QuantityValue.\n\nNow check if any missing obligations: also need to ensure that ruleLength property is of type QuantityValue maybe domain/range already defined elsewhere but SHACL should enforce.\n\nThus at least two issues.\n\nNo material questions; gaps are unresolved source context but not code defects; they affect assessment? Gaps are about missing source sections, but not code. According to schema, if gaps material then HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED. Gaps are in retrieval_gaps list (G1..G5). They are about source completeness, not code issues. According to instructions, gap_review must be answered. In response, we must include gap_review array with each G id and material boolean and why.\n\nWe need to decide material: Are these gaps material to code correctness? They refer to source sections missing; but code shape does not depend on those missing source texts. The requirement representation maybe incomplete due to missing source but not code defect. I'd mark them as nonmaterial (material false) and explain.\n\nThus gap_review entries for G1..G5 with material false.\n\nNow construct assessment: Since there are actionable code defects, we must REJECT? Actually assessment: APPROVE requires no issues. REJECT needs actionable code issue. Yes we have issues, so REJECT.\n\nProvide issues array with description, evidence maybe use evidence IDs maybe none? We can reference E? We could use [] empty? Must have at least one evidence ID. Could cite E331 which contains the quotation of the requirement. Use that.\n\nIssue 1: Missing class constraint for ruleLength node.\n\nIssue 2: nodeKind too restrictive, should allow blank node.\n\nProvide suggestions.\n\nNow construct JSON.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_8d221cf37bfbeca1","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"REJECT\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"The shape does not enforce that the value of `vocab:ruleLength` is a `qudt:QuantityValue`. The requirement states that the value must be a QUDT QuantityValue, but the SHACL only checks for the presence of `qudt:numericValue` and `qudt:unit` without asserting the class of the node.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"E331\"\n      ],\n      \"location\": {\n        \"start\": 20,\n        \"end\": 20,\n        \"unit\": \"lines\"\n      },\n      \"suggestion\": \"Add a `sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;` statement inside the nested `sh:node` block (e.g., after line 21) to ensure the node is of type `qudt:QuantityValue`.\",\n      \"operands\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"`sh:nodeKind sh:IRI` forces the `vocab:ruleLength` value to be an IRI node. In many RDF models a `qudt:QuantityValue` is represented as a blank node, so this restriction may reject valid data.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"E331\"\n      ],\n      \"location\": {\n        \"start\": 20,\n        \"end\": 20,\n        \"unit\": \"lines\"\n      },\n      \"suggestion\": \"Replace `sh:nodeKind sh:IRI` with `sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI` (or remove the constraint entirely, as the added `sh:class` will already restrict the node type).\",\n      \"operands\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"gap_review\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G1\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing section 10 in the source document does not affect the SHACL shape; the shape only encodes the structural constraints for `ruleLength`.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G2\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing section 3 is unrelated to the definition of `ruleLength` and therefore does not impact the current SHACL.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G3\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The ambiguous table 3 reference does not contain constraints needed for this shape.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G4\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The ambiguous table 6 reference does not affect the ruleLength constraints.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G5\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing external document (UR P0) is not required for validating the `ruleLength` property in this SH